# Copy to .env. `pnpm start`, `pnpm dev` and `pnpm concord` read it; a container gets these from
# its platform instead. Everything is optional: with nothing set, Concord serves mainnet and
# testnet on http://127.0.0.1:4400 and keeps its data under ./data.

# ── where it runs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONCORD_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Falls back to PORT, then 4400.
CONCORD_PORT=4400
# The address people open. Decides cookie security and the Google redirect URI. Must be https
# for anything beyond your own machine. On Render it defaults to the service's own URL, which
# Render sets as RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL.
# CONCORD_PUBLIC_URL=https://concord.example.com
# Reverse proxies in front of Concord whose X-Forwarded-For entry is believed (for rate limits).
# CONCORD_TRUST_PROXY=1
# The built dashboard served at /. Defaults to apps/web/dist in the checkout.
# CONCORD_WEB_DIR=/srv/concord/web

# ── data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Holds control.db (accounts, workspaces, sessions) and one database per workspace under orgs/.
# Must be a local disk: SQLite's write-ahead log does not work over NFS.
# CONCORD_DATA_DIR=./data
# Set when the host discards that directory on restart, so the dashboard warns users.
# CONCORD_EPHEMERAL=1

# ── who may sign up ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# open: anyone may create a workspace. code: only with a code from `pnpm concord signup-code`.
CONCORD_SIGNUP=open
# Assets one workspace may watch.
# CONCORD_MAX_ASSETS=10
# Work factors for password hashing, as scrypt N:r:p. The default is 32768:8:3. On a host with
# very little CPU a sign-in can take seconds; measure there before lowering it, and not below
# 16384:8:1. Existing passwords keep working whatever this is set to.
# CONCORD_PASSWORD_COST=32768:8:3
# Google sign-in is offered only when both are set. Create an OAuth client (type "Web
# application") with the redirect URI <CONCORD_PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/google/callback.
# CONCORD_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# CONCORD_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Stellar ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The network a new visitor sees first: mainnet or testnet. Both are always served.
# CONCORD_DEFAULT_NETWORK=mainnet
# Comma-separated, tried in order; a failing or rate-limited endpoint is rested and the next
# used. Mainnet defaults to free public endpoints, which suit light use. SDF runs no public
# mainnet RPC, so point this at a provider for anything more.
# CONCORD_MAINNET_RPC_URLS=https://your-provider.example/stellar-rpc
# CONCORD_TESTNET_RPC_URLS=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# CONCORD_MAINNET_HORIZON_URLS=https://horizon.stellar.org
# CONCORD_TESTNET_HORIZON_URLS=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
# Headers for providers that authenticate by header, keyed by host.
# CONCORD_RPC_HEADERS={"your-provider.example":{"x-api-key":"..."}}
# Seconds between background indexer passes. 0 turns it off.
CONCORD_SYNC_INTERVAL=30

# ── command line ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The workspace `pnpm concord` acts on when --org is not given: its id or exact name.
# CONCORD_ORG=
